  "relationships": {
    "_description": "Key relationships between entities. Keep these in mind when designing the backend.",
    "diagram": [
      "content  --belongs_to-->  category  (many-to-one via category_id)",
      "content  --tagged_with-->  tags  (many-to-many, simple string array for now)",
      "content  --taught_by-->  instructor  (many-to-one, embedded for now)",
      "collection  --contains-->  content  (many-to-many via content_ids array)",
      "user_progress  --tracks-->  content × user  (one per user per content)",
      "user_stats  --aggregates-->  user_progress  (computed, not stored separately early on)",
      "conversation  --belongs_to-->  user  (one active conversation, history saved)",
      "today.sections[].items  --references-->  content  (via content_id)"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Everything links back to 'content' via content_id — this is the backbone of the app.",
      "Today tab sections are server-driven: the backend decides what to show and in what order.",
      "Collections can be both curated (editorial) and auto-generated (personalized).",
      "User progress is the key table for personalization — it powers streaks, recommendations, and 'continue listening'.",
      "Luma conversations reference content_ids when recommending sessions, creating a link between chat and library."
    ]
  }
}
